# Area reviewer assignment
#
# Used by .github/workflows/area-reviewers.yml. Unlike CODEOWNERS (which
# requests review from a whole team, where it is easy for everyone to assume
# someone else will look), this file maps paths to *groups*, and the workflow
# picks ONE concrete person from each matching group, requests their review,
# assigns them to the PR, and leaves a comment explaining why they were chosen.
#
# Syntax
# ------
#
#   group <name> = @user1 @user2 ...
#       Defines a group of individual GitHub users. A group may be defined
#       across multiple lines; members accumulate. A group with no members
#       is ignored (handy for areas that are not staffed yet).
#
#   strategy = least-loaded | round-robin | random
#       How to pick a member (default: least-loaded).
#         least-loaded - member with the fewest open PRs in this repo that are
#                        currently awaiting their review (ties broken by
#                        round-robin).
#         round-robin  - rotate through members by PR number.
#         random       - uniformly random member.
#
#   <pattern> <group> [<group> ...]
#       Path rule using CODEOWNERS/gitignore-style patterns:
#         - A leading "/" anchors the pattern at the repository root.
#         - A pattern with no "/" (other than a trailing one) matches at any
#           depth, e.g. "*.proto".
#         - A trailing "/" (or a pattern naming a directory) matches
#           everything beneath it.
#         - "*" matches within a path segment, "**" matches across segments,
#           "?" matches a single character.
#
#       NOTE: unlike CODEOWNERS, ALL matching rules apply (not just the last
#       one), so a PR that touches both storage code and a .proto file gets
#       one storage reviewer and one API reviewer.
#
# The PR author is never selected. If someone already assigned to, requested
# on, or reviewing the PR is a member of a matching group, that group is
# considered covered and nobody new is selected for it. Selections are
# recorded in the bot comment and are not re-rolled on later pushes; delete
# the comment to force a re-roll on the next push.
#
# Only list individual users (not teams) as group members.

strategy = least-loaded

# --- Groups -----------------------------------------------------------------
# TODO: fill in members, e.g. `group api-reviewers = @alice @bob`.

group api-reviewers = @jterry75
group storage =
group networking =
group vmbus =
group hypervisor =

# --- Rules ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Protobuf / ttrpc API surfaces
*.proto                         api-reviewers
/vm/devices/get/underhill_config/ api-reviewers

# Storage
/vm/devices/storage/            storage

# Networking
/vm/devices/net/                networking

# VMBus
/vm/devices/vmbus/              vmbus

# Hypervisor / virtualization backends
/vm/hv1/                        hypervisor
/vm/kvm/                        hypervisor
/vm/whp/                        hypervisor
/vmm_core/virt*/                hypervisor
/openhcl/virt_mshv_vtl/         hypervisor
